title An ask lives 104 minutes on the one surface Keaton reads
prompt the baton -- grass, auditing lane, lap 4575
rota lap 4575, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; its threshold asks a lap to record the silences as well as the sounds, which is what sent this lap looking for the question nobody answered
think My own last lap found a scan header saying its question was asked on ITINERARY when the ask was no longer there. That was one lantern. This lap asked how large the class is.
think A ship writes its question for Keaton inside its account block on the live card. tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh moves that block WHOLE onto a shelf so the card holds under its bound -- correct, and the question rides along.
think Measured the population from the shelves themselves: 72 **YOURS asks across 54 of 339 account shelves, and a grep for **YOURS under tools/ returns one line of unrelated prose, so nothing in the tree reads a shelf for a question.
think Measured the lifetime from consecutive same-seat shelf stamps: 292 lives, median 104.4 minutes, p25 69.5, p75 159.1, and 283 of 292 under eight hours. A question written in the night reaches a shelf before morning.
think Of the eight asks living on the card, exactly one was carried forward by the ship that wrote it -- checked by matching each living ask's own text against the shelves.
think The repair a lap may make without Keaton's word is to give the move a voice: the writer prints asks_shelved=<n> and one ask: line per question. It edits nothing, judges nothing, and refuses nothing new, because answering an ask is his word.
think The count reads the whole block before the listing truncates, since a truncating reader reporting its own truncation as the finding is a fault this tree booked at head -40 on my own lap two days ago.
obs First resident on live state: shelving my own elder GRASS block through the changed writer printed my own unanswered dated_path ask back at me.
obs Both mutations bite -- a count taken from the bounded listing misses a seventeenth ask (43 to 41), and a silent dry run loses three legs (43 to 35). The witness itself reds on a silenced tool and greens on its return, proven on metal in both directions.
obs Grading the touched header raised it from C+/79 to B+/85, which closed the molt frame the reading pushed. The witness reads B/80.
obs The standing population is reported by the witness and gated at nothing. A guard that reddened on an unanswered question would red on ordinary work, which is a guard someone turns off.
